<title>UK: Glaxo's Imigran nasal spray gets EU nod.</title>
<headline>Glaxo's Imigran nasal spray gets EU nod.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Glaxo Wellcome Plc said on Wednesday that Imigran (sumatriptan) nasal spray, a new formulation of its migraine treatment, has been cleared for regulatory approval under the European Commission's mutual recognition procedure in 12 countries.  </p>
<p>Glaxo said marketing applications for Imigran nasal spray have been submitted to other regulatory authorities around the world.</p>
<p>The pharmaceutical firm said that Imigran is the only 5-HT agonist to be licensed for the acute treatment of migraine.</p>
<p>Imigran is marketed in oral and injection form in over 70 countries worldwide and sales of Imigran for the six months to July 1996 were 263 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
</text>
